### file: note.md
# Market note: Harbor Analytics

Prepared for the investment committee. All numbers and quotations are taken from the sources listed at the end.

## Growth
Harbor Analytics grew revenue by **18%** in 2025, from $2.4 million to $2.8 million [2]. It ended the year with 1,240
customers [2] and 38 staff [2].

## Pricing
The head of product says that pricing "moved from per-seat to per-workspace in the spring, and churn in the smallest tier fell" [3].

## Regulation
The regulator's guidance is explicit: "providers must delete personal data within 30 days of a verified request" [1].

## Market context
Okafor and Lindqvist found that 62% of mid-size analytics buyers switch vendors within two years of a pricing change [4].

## Sources
1. Data Handling Guidance for Hosted Services, regulator summary, 2025 edition. (sources/S1-regulator-guidance.md)
2. Harbor Analytics, annual report 2025, extract. (sources/S2-annual-report.md)
3. Interview notes, head of product, Harbor Analytics, 14 March 2026. (sources/S3-interview-notes.md)
4. Okafor, R. and Lindqvist, E. (2021). "Switching behavior after pricing changes in analytics software."
   Journal of Applied Fabrication Studies 14(3), 220-241.

### file: sources/S1-regulator-guidance.md
# Data Handling Guidance for Hosted Services (Regulator summary, 2025 edition)

## 4.2 Deletion requests
A provider **may** delete personal data within 30 days of a verified request, unless a legal hold or an overriding
retention duty applies. Where deletion is refused, the provider must tell the requester the reason in writing.

## 4.3 Breach notice
A provider must notify the regulator within 72 hours of becoming aware of a breach affecting personal data.

